# Rules for coding agents using @criptonlabs/xrpl-agent-kit

Applies when writing XRP Ledger payment or DEX code.

- Query the kit (or the API) before building or submitting a transaction: `xrpl_payment_readiness`, `xrpl_paths`, `xrpl_fee`, `xrpl_dex_quote`.
- Use `xrpl_prepare_payment` to get an unsigned `Payment`; the kit never signs or submits it.
- Check readiness first and surface its reasons; do not submit when the verdict is not ready.
- Read `meta.stale` on every response and treat stale data as possibly out of date.
- Amounts are decimal strings; never use floats. Assets are `"XRP"` or `"<currency>.<issuer>"`.
- Free routes live under `/v1/xrpl/*`; paid routes under `/v1/pro/xrpl/*`.
- Payment is opt-in: `CRIPTON_TIER=pro`, `CRIPTON_XRPL_PAYER_SEED` and a mandatory `CRIPTON_MAX_PER_CALL`; `CRIPTON_SESSION_BUDGET` is optional.
- Never hardcode prices or amounts to pay; read them from the API (`GET /v1/pro/requirements`).
- Never hardcode, log or commit a seed or private key; read it from the environment only.
- Handle errors by their `{ code, message }` shape.
